    description: "**Origin.** Filed 2026-05-30 as a sub-META of INV-fabov following the linked-pile L1 investigation. Sub-META B.\n\n**The shape.** Five active items describe argparse-layer type/range validation gaps. CLI flags that accept any string are not type-checked; numeric flags that should reject `<0` / `>1` / `max<min` combinations don't. Same root: no shared argparse-action factory for \"bounded numeric\" / \"validated path\" / \"positive-int\" types — each subcommand reinvents.\n\n**Fix shape.** A common argparse-action factory: `bounded_int(min=0, max=...)`, `validated_path(must_exist=True, must_be_dir=False, ...)`, `positive_count(...)`. Plus argparse-type wrappers at each subcommand. Each member item becomes one wiring patch.\n\n**Members (5).** WI-vusaf (compact --max-symbols/--coverage/--negative-limits, canonical after INV-nonag duplicate-close), INV-toniv (search negative `--limit` accepted silently), INV-jibof (positional path silently swallows non-directory), INV-fapid (slice `--out slice.json` silently overridden by argparse-default), and the `--limit` slice of INV-votop (the type/range face; the registry-membership face goes to sub-META C).\n\n**Note on INV-votop.** This is the only multi-face item: `--kind` and `--language` are registry-membership (sub-META C); `--limit` is type/range (here). Item gets primary parent = sub-META C with a cross-reference discussion to sub-META B for the `--limit` face.\n\n**Parent:** INV-fabov-kapit-mupit-tigoz-lurol-mulus-jivik-kajun."  # 4ac7
    fields:  # 4ac7
      statement: "Every numeric / path / typed CLI flag must have argparse-layer validation (type-cast, range-check, existence-check); no flag may silently accept out-of-range or wrong-type values."  # 4ac7
      root_cause: "No shared argparse-action factory for bounded-numeric / validated-path / positive-int types — each subcommand reinvents. Symptoms: compact accepts max<min and coverage>1 (WI-vusaf), search accepts negative --limit (INV-toniv), positional path silently swallows non-directory (INV-jibof), slice --out silently overridden by argparse-default (INV-fapid)."  # 4ac7
